--TEST--
A `catch` binding is not readable after its clause — only the thrown value assigns it (`rule:types/declaration`'s `catch` row)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `$e` is a local of the enclosing function, declared by the clause, but the
// only thing that ever assigns it is the value being caught. No path out of
// the `try` carries one — not even when the clause is the only way the
// statement finishes normally — so a read after it is refused here rather
// than reaching the lowerer as a name it has never been given.
try {
    throw new LogicError("inside");
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
echo $e->message, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0301]: `$e` is read before any assignment reaches it
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
